Let $\boldsymbol{G}\sim\mathrm{SBM}(n, d, \lambda)$ for any $d\geqslant 1$.
        There exist universal constants $C_1$ and $C_2$ such that for any $\varepsilon \geqslant C_1 \cdot \left( \frac{C_2 + \log d}{d} \right)^{1/3}$, with high probability over $\boldsymbol{G}$, we can partition the edge set $E(\boldsymbol{G})$ as $E(\boldsymbol{G}_1) \sqcup E(\boldsymbol{G}_2)$ for graphs $\boldsymbol{G}_1$ and $\boldsymbol{G}_2$ on $[n]$ where:
        \begin{enumerate}
            \item  The maximum degree of $\boldsymbol{G}_1$ is at most $(1+\varepsilon)d$.
            \item  $\boldsymbol{G}_2$ is a $\left\lparen \Delta, D \right\rparen$-pseudorandom near-forest with respect to $S\coloneqq V'(\boldsymbol{G}_1)\cap V'(\boldsymbol{G}_2)$ for $\Delta = o(\log n)$ and $D = (1+\varepsilon)d$.
        \end{enumerate}

